<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bytom</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bytom is a city in the Silesian Voivodeship of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and one of the oldest towns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a>. It grew around an early medieval stronghold, received town rights in 1254 and from 1281 was the seat of the Piast Duchy of Bytom. Rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>, lead and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, it became a major mining and industrial city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bytom.jpg" alt="Bytom" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adrian Tync · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bytom_Rynek_aerial_2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
